{
  "example": "{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.agent-harness.agent_config`\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.agent-harness.with_agent`\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.validation-cache.with_agent`\n\nThis Bedrock configuration selects a model, AWS profile, and region for the\ndomain's cache:\n\n```rust,ignore\nuse trust_but_verify::agent::AgentConfig;\nuse trust_but_verify::agent::BedrockConfig;\nuse trust_but_verify::domain::ValidationCache;\n\nlet config = AgentConfig::Bedrock(\n    BedrockConfig::new(\"us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-5-5\".into())\n        .aws_profile(\"development\".into())\n        .region(\"us-east-1\".into()),\n);\nlet cache = ValidationCache::<AppDomain>::with_agent(config);\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The example `requirements.sdk.graph.agent-harness.setup` is a concrete case. It builds an `AgentConfig::Bedrock` from `BedrockConfig::new(\"us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-5-5\")` with profile \"development\" and region \"us-east-1\", then passes it to `ValidationCache::<AppDomain>::with_agent(config)`. The expected outcome is that the cache carries the selected model, profile and region. The cited requirements add that the cache is empty, that its clones share the agent, and that the SDK does not persist the configuration.\n\nThe only `{test}` reference to the example is `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/configured.rs#mod[tests]/fn[bedrock_configuration_attaches_to_a_cache_without_being_persisted]`. It builds the same Bedrock config and calls `ValidationCache::with_agent(config.clone())`. It then checks each outcome:\n- **Config attached:** `assert_eq!(domain.cache().agent...backend, config)` shows the cache holds the exact model, profile and region.\n- **Empty cache:** the `outlines` map is empty and `sources` is `None`.\n- **Shared by clones:** `Arc::ptr_eq` shows a cloned domain shares the same agent.\n- **Usable through the cache:** a `Validator::refresh_evidence` call runs a criterion through the cache. The `Question` criterion with `false` does not call the agent, so this only shows the cache works. It does not show the agent being used, and backend setup is deferred.\n- **Not persisted:** the saved record serialized to JSON has no `backend` field and contains neither \"development\" nor \"claude-sonnet\".\n\nThe test helpers (`TestDomain`, `Question`) are simple and behave as the assertions assume. I found no behavior that would violate the example and still pass these tests.",
